Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: build the Docker image in /src with Go 1.26

The source was copied to /go, which is $GOPATH, so Go ignored go.mod
("go: warning: ignoring go.mod in $GOPATH"). golang:1.26.1 sets
GOTOOLCHAIN=local while go.mod requires Go 1.26.2, so the module build
fails too. Same fix as in openuem-console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i1yNq2pA1uqE9wBGDr
---
 Dockerfile | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index cea26f2..297c024 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
-FROM golang:1.26.1 AS build
+FROM golang:1.26 AS build
+WORKDIR /src
 COPY . ./
 RUN go build -o /bin/openuem-worker .
 
